    <string name="exclude_pattern_help_title">Exclude pattern guide</string>
    <string name="exclude_pattern_help_message">Exclude patterns are passed to tar as --exclude arguments. Supported modes:\n\n1. Exact match: enter a file or directory name\n   e.g. cache, temp.txt\n\n2. Wildcards:\n   • * matches any characters except /\n     e.g. *.log, cache/*\n   • ? matches a single character\n     e.g. file?.txt\n   • ** matches any characters including /\n     e.g. **/cache/**\n\n3. Path matching:\n   • Relative path from the backup root\n     e.g. files/cache, shared_prefs/*.xml\n   • Absolute path (not recommended)\n\nExamples:\n• cache - exclude directories named cache\n• *.tmp - exclude temporary files\n• files/logs/* - exclude all files under logs\n• **/thumbnail* - exclude thumbnail-related files\n\nNote: patterns apply during packaging; excluded files are not backed up.</string>
